### Quick demo of the whole flow (VS Code "REST Client" or IntelliJ HTTP client).
### Run the requests top to bottom and paste the tokens/ids you get back into the variables.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@ownerToken = PASTE_OWNER_TOKEN
@customerToken = PASTE_CUSTOMER_TOKEN
@restaurantId = 1
@menuItemId = 1
@orderId = 1

### 1. Register a restaurant owner
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Olivia Owner", "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "password123", "role": "RESTAURANT_OWNER" }

### 2. Register a customer
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Chris Customer", "email": "customer@example.com", "password": "password123", "role": "CUSTOMER" }

### 3. Login (returns a JWT)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "customer@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### 4. Owner creates a restaurant
POST {{host}}/api/restaurants
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Spice Hub", "description": "North Indian", "city": "Delhi" }

### 5. Owner adds a menu item
POST {{host}}/api/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Paneer Tikka", "description": "Starter", "price": 149.50, "available": true }

### 6. Anyone can browse (search, filter by city, paginate, sort)
GET {{host}}/api/restaurants?city=Delhi&q=spice&page=0&size=10&sortBy=name&direction=asc

### 7. Customer adds to cart
POST {{host}}/api/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "menuItemId": {{menuItemId}}, "quantity": 2 }

### 8. Customer places the order
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "deliveryAddress": "12 MG Road, Delhi" }

### 9. Owner moves the order forward (PLACED -> CONFIRMED -> PREPARING -> OUT_FOR_DELIVERY -> DELIVERED)
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CONFIRMED" }

### 10. Customer views their orders
GET {{host}}/api/orders/my
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 11. Owner views orders for their restaurant
GET {{host}}/api/orders/restaurant/{{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
